---
import { ArrowUpRight, FlaskConical, Lightbulb } from '@lucide/astro'
import { site } from '../config/site'
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro'

const streams = [
  {
    eyebrow: '01 / THE EXPERIMENT',
    title: 'The Lab',
    subtitle: 'One Human. AI in the Loop.',
    paragraphs: [
      'A practical experiment exploring what one person can build with AI and what that means for the future of software engineering and business.',
      "I'm documenting the journey from idea to working software, including the architecture, engineering, decisions, mistakes, costs and lessons learned.",
      "The objective isn't to prove that AI can replace people. It's to understand how AI changes what's possible, and where human judgement and accountability remain essential.",
    ],
    cta: 'Follow the Experiment',
    href: site.labSection || site.publication,
    Icon: FlaskConical,
  },
  {
    eyebrow: '02 / THE THINKING',
    title: 'Perspectives',
    subtitle: 'Ideas, observations and questions worth exploring.',
    paragraphs: [
      'My reflections on business, technology, AI, leadership, people and the changing world.',
      "Sometimes inspired by what's happening in The Lab. Sometimes by something I've read, experienced or observed.",
      'Not every article needs to reach a conclusion. Some are simply about asking better questions.',
    ],
    cta: 'Explore Perspectives',
    href: site.perspectivesSection || site.publication,
    Icon: Lightbulb,
  },
]
---
<section class="section writing-section" id="writing" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="writing-intro">
      <div class="section-topline"><SectionHeading label="WRITING & IDEAS" title="Ideas worth exploring." id="writing-title" /><span class="section-number" aria-hidden="true">02 / 03</span></div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>I write about the things that interest me, challenge my thinking and occasionally change my mind.</p>
        <p>Some ideas come from practical experimentation. Others come from experience, observation or simply being curious about the world around us.</p>
        <p>This is where I explore those ideas, ask questions and share what I learn.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="writing-grid">
      {streams.map(({ eyebrow, title, subtitle, paragraphs, cta, href, Icon }) => (
        <article class="writing-card">
          <div class="writing-card-top">
            <span class="writing-card-eyebrow">{eyebrow}</span>
            <span class="icon-box"><Icon size={22} stroke-width={1.5} aria-hidden="true" /></span>
          </div>
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p class="writing-card-subtitle">{subtitle}</p>
          <div class="writing-card-copy">
            {paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
          </div>
          <a class="writing-card-link" href={href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{cta} <ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <article class="writing-card featured-article" aria-labelledby="lab-article-title">
      <p class="writing-card-eyebrow">THE LAB &middot; TECHNOLOGY DELIVERY &amp; AI</p>
      <h3 id="lab-article-title">The LAB: The Changing Economics of Technology Delivery</h3>
      <div class="writing-card-copy">
        <p>AI is challenging the economics of technology delivery. Can one person, supported by AI, deliver what once required an entire technology team? The LAB is a practical experiment exploring how AI changes the cost, speed, quality and skills required to build software — and what that means for the future of technology organisations.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="writing-card-link" href="https://vicusbrits.substack.com/p/the-lab-the-changing-economics-of" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the full article on Substack <ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="writing-card featured-article" aria-labelledby="latest-perspectives-title">
      <p class="writing-card-eyebrow">PERSPECTIVES &middot; SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</p>
      <h3 id="latest-perspectives-title">I Built a Website I Don't Know How to Maintain. And That's Fine.</h3>
      <p class="writing-card-subtitle">But would I run a bank that way?</p>
      <div class="writing-card-copy">
        <p>AI helped me build a website I couldn't maintain on my own. That's fine for a personal project, but what about critical financial systems? As AI changes how we build software, it raises a difficult question: how much understanding can we safely trade for speed, and what controls do we need in its place?</p>
      </div>
      <a class="writing-card-link" href="https://vicusbrits.substack.com/p/i-built-a-website-i-dont-know-how" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the full article on Substack <ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="writing-card featured-article" aria-labelledby="agile-waterfall-title">
      <p class="writing-card-eyebrow">PERSPECTIVES &middot; SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</p>
      <h3 id="agile-waterfall-title">Now That Cars Can Fly, Do We Still Need Agile and Waterfall?</h3>
      <p class="writing-card-subtitle">AI gave software development wings. Are we still managing traffic lights?</p>
      <div class="writing-card-copy">
        <p>AI is dramatically changing how quickly we can build software. But are our development methodologies keeping up?</p>
        <p>Clear requirements suddenly matter more, while rapid AI-generated solutions introduce new questions about architecture, quality and accountability.</p>
        <p>Perhaps the real opportunity isn't choosing between Agile and Waterfall, but fundamentally rethinking how we build software.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="writing-card-link" href="https://vicusbrits.substack.com/p/now-that-cars-can-fly-do-we-still" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the full article on Substack <ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
    </article>
    <div class="newsletter">
      <div>
        <h3>Follow the thinking. Follow the experiment.</h3>
        <p>Two streams of writing. One exploring what we can build. The other exploring what we think, question and learn along the way.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button-primary" href={site.publication} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read &amp; Subscribe on Substack <ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
